cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  nf-claw was created by Danilo Monge. The pipelines it serves are authored by
  the nf-core community — the core of the library — and are wrapped unmodified;
  nf-claw also adapts some files and its repository structure from ClawBio
  (created by Manuel Corpas). If you use nf-claw, please cite it using the
  metadata below, together with Nextflow, the nf-core framework, and especially
  the specific nf-core pipeline you ran (see references).
type: software
title: "nf-claw: A self-maintaining, token-minimal library of nf-core pipelines for AI agents"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-06-15"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  nf-claw turns nf-core pipelines into an agent-runnable library. The pipelines
  themselves are authored by the nf-core community and wrapped unmodified as
  git submodules pinned to a release tag; nf-claw pairs each with an
  generated skill.md describing declared inputs and run commands, and a full
  parameter reference.md. Context comes from the pinned schemas and source,
  with documented exact-schema audits correcting stale input contracts. A
  generic runner launches supported pipelines and records a provenance bundle;
  curated handoff rules connect pipelines, and documented runtime corrections
  are applied through recorded configurations without editing upstream source.
  scheduled workflows check new upstream releases and regenerate context.
  Validation and replay checks cover declared dependencies and observed
  execution behavior, rather than certifying biological accuracy.
keywords:
  - nextflow
  - nf-core
  - bioinformatics
  - pipelines
  - workflows
  - AI agents
  - reproducibility
  - automation
authors:
  - family-names: Monge
    given-names: Danilo
    affiliation: "Eberhard Karls Universität Tübingen"
